# Per-Dockerfile ignore file: `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` takes precedence over
# a context-root `.dockerignore`, keeping every Docker artifact under docker/.
# Patterns are relative to the build context — the repo root, since compose
# builds with `context: ..` — NOT to docker/.
#
# Build-context bloat guard: keep the 2.5 GB cargo target/, node_modules trees,
# local state and dotenv files out of the tar stream. Nested paths need `**/`:
# a bare name matches the context root only (`target` alone leaves
# apps/runner/target in the context — bare matching verified against
# moby/patternmatcher semantics).
#
# Keep in sync with docker/Dockerfile.runner.dockerignore (both prod images
# build from the repo root); the dev images use the minimal variants.

# language build output
**/target
**/dist
**/out

# dependencies
**/node_modules

# container registry seeds + local state
**/.wrangler
**/.celld
data
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-wal

# vcs / editor
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/*.dockerignore
**/.idea

# dotenv files MUST use `**/`: a bare name only matches the context root, and
# `apps/noite/.dev.vars` is a real secret file (this image bakes it into the
# worker bundle's vars block if it leaks into the context).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars.*
!**/.dev.vars.example

# plan + docs are repo content — keep markdown out of images to shrink context
# (README is small; SPEC.md is small; both fine to exclude since no image COPYs them)
**/*.md
**/*.mdx
